# Commit Message Rules (full doc: docs/commit-message.md)

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>
```

## Types

feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore

## Rules

- Imperative mood: "add" not "added"
- Don't capitalize first letter
- No period at the end
- Max 72 characters first line
- Use body for "why", footer for issue refs

## Examples

```
feat(auth): add recovery phrase login
fix(posts): correct timestamp formatting in feed
refactor(core): extract user validation to pipe
```

For full guide with scopes, multi-line examples, and breaking changes: read docs/commit-message.md
